{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"199f7bcf4dac500b","x":-300,"y":-200,"width":880,"height":600,"type":"text","text":"Armount:\n\nArmount is an ancient civilization from 1000 P.D.\n\nArmount was a city fully of arcanists of all different types and is the main cause for all arcane research to this point. What once was this great city in the current time is a wasted gargantuan landscape of endless ruins and arcane horrors. \n\nArmount began to rise in place far north east of what is currently Volstar. This city rose as a response to the wave of dunamantic energy created when the Raven Queen ascended to God hood. Armount was founded by a man named Iltar Armount, Iltar brought together the brightest minds in Villatos in a hope to harness this strange new power that was washed across the entire world. \n\nArmount began its rise in 950 P.D, This city floating in the sky using a material known as brimstone was kilometers in height, width and length. Armount is the largest civilization ever created. \n\nIltar and the rest of the Dunamis ward spent their lives researching this mysterious magic naming it Dunamancy. Their research uncovered that Dunamancy started from a relic but they were never able to find it and so they attempted to re-create it. These experiments were very unethical, human trials to see how dunamis effects the soul, implanting residuum enhanced by Dunamis and many other awful experiments took place in the Dunamis ward all under the leadership of Iltar. \n\nUpon discovering the research of the Dunamis ward and its unethical practices other political leaders and wards a like questioned Iltar and backed him into a corner and they attempted a cue. Because of this backlash Iltar attempted to fast track his work and create a replica of the ancient artifact before he knew how and as a result the entire city was destroyed and the ruins of it are forever plagued by arcane horrors.\n"},
		{"id":"0d61c5f16657c2e5","x":-40,"y":-375,"width":500,"height":155,"type":"text","text":"Verazanoths plot:\n\nPateintly waiting for the Armountians to destroy themselves and giving Iltar what he needed to go to the Shadow fell where he became the perfect vessel for The Whispered One.\n"},
		{"id":"705c36612286c8ba","x":-425,"y":-435,"width":285,"height":138,"type":"text","text":"[[The Age of Arcanum.canvas]]\n[[Iltar Armount.canvas]]\n[[Verazanoth.canvas]]\n[[The Whispered One.canvas]]\n#Lore "}
	],
